Fix SSE2 pcmp_lt<Packet2l> comparing low 32-bit halves as signed

Backport of upstream Eigen commit 8cef20fd ("Core: Fix SSE2
pcmp_lt<Packet2l> comparing low halves as signed", libeigen/eigen!2831),
adapted to the 5.0.1 release which predates the SIGN_MASK_I32 macro.

Without SSE4.2 the 64-bit compare is emulated from two 32-bit compares,
but the low half was compared signed. This misorders positive int64
values whose low word has bit 31 set (e.g. 2147483649), producing wrong
Clip and Sign results. Biasing only the low lanes by 2^31 makes one
signed 32-bit compare serve as an unsigned compare for the low half. The
0x80000000 lane mask matches the idiom already used elsewhere in this
file (e.g. pabs).

--- a/Eigen/src/Core/arch/SSE/PacketMath.h
+++ b/Eigen/src/Core/arch/SSE/PacketMath.h
@@ -947,7 +947,10 @@ EIGEN_STRONG_INLINE Packet2l pcmp_lt(const Packet2l& a, const Packet2l& b) {
 #else
   Packet4i eq = pcmp_eq<Packet4i>(Packet4i(a), Packet4i(b));
   Packet2l hi_eq = Packet2l(_mm_shuffle_epi32(eq, (shuffle_mask<1, 1, 3, 3>::mask)));
-  Packet4i lt = pcmp_lt<Packet4i>(Packet4i(a), Packet4i(b));
+  // The low halves carry magnitude only and must be ordered as unsigned, while the high halves carry
+  // the sign. Biasing just the low lanes by 2^31 makes one signed 32-bit compare serve both.
+  const Packet4i kLowSignFlip = _mm_setr_epi32(0x80000000, 0x0, 0x80000000, 0x0);
+  Packet4i lt = pcmp_lt<Packet4i>(pxor(Packet4i(a), kLowSignFlip), pxor(Packet4i(b), kLowSignFlip));
   Packet2l hi_lt = Packet2l(_mm_shuffle_epi32(lt, (shuffle_mask<1, 1, 3, 3>::mask)));
   Packet2l lo_lt = Packet2l(_mm_shuffle_epi32(lt, (shuffle_mask<0, 0, 2, 2>::mask)));
   // return hi(a) < hi(b) || (hi(a) == hi(b) && lo(a) < lo(b))
